course: dictionary
lesson: 11473
title: Aerial: from the air, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Aerial is one of them. When you meet it, read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «The aerial photo shows the whole town from high above.» Here the photo was taken from the air, so aerial means from the air.
explain: Look at the other clues too. «Dad climbed the ladder to fix the TV aerial on our roof.» A TV aerial is a wire or rod that picks up TV signals. Ladder and roof are the clues that tell you it is not a view from the sky.
explain: Aerial also means in the air. «The skier did an aerial flip off the big jump.» Here the words skier and jump tell you the aerial is a trick done in the air during a sport. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Aerial means from the air or in the air.
fact: An aerial is a wire or rod that sends or picks up radio or TV signals.
fact: In the US, a TV aerial is called an antenna.
fact: An aerial photograph is taken from a plane or a drone, so it shows a place from above.
fact: In sport, an aerial is a jump with a flip in the air, as in skiing or snowboarding.
exercise: «The aerial photo shows the whole town from high above.» What does aerial mean here? | Under the ground | Very loud | *From the air, seen from high above | Made of glass
exercise: «Dad climbed the ladder to fix the TV aerial.» What is an aerial here? | *A wire or rod that picks up TV signals | A type of car | A rung on the ladder | A kind of bird
exercise: In the US, a TV aerial is called what? | A shelf | A rope | A bell | *An antenna
test: «The skier flew off the ramp and did an aerial with a flip.» In sport, what is an aerial? | *A jump with a flip in the air | A wooden sled | A type of goggles | A slow walk down the slope
test: Which phrase means a view of a place from high up? | Garden gate | *Aerial view | Sea bed | Underground tunnel
exam: «Our drone took an aerial photograph of the school field.» What does aerial photograph mean? | A photo of a bird's nest | A blurry photo of a face | A photo taken under water | *A photo taken from the air
